name			rtl8814au
version			0.1.1-1
architecture	x86_64
summary			"RTL8814AU USB WiFi driver (unofficial)"

description		"Native Haiku kernel driver for USB WiFi adapters based on
the Realtek RTL8814AU chipset (4x4 802.11ac, used in adapters like the
ASUS USB-AC68 and Edimax EW-7833UAC).

Supports open and WPA2-PSK (AES/CCMP) networks via an in-driver 4-way
handshake (the standard Haiku wpa_supplicant path has a stack-level issue
with EAPOL delivery on AF_LINK that prevents conventional drivers from
completing WPA2 association).  CCMP encrypt/decrypt for the data path is
performed in software inside the driver — the chip's HW crypto engine
refuses to engage on Haiku and the SW fallback is what makes WPA2 work
end-to-end.

To join a WPA2-PSK network, run the bundled `wifi-join` tool — neither
`ifconfig <dev> join SSID password` nor the Deskbar Network app can
deliver the passphrase to the driver, so the helper is currently the
only path that completes the handshake:

  wifi-join /dev/net/rtl8814au/0 <ssid> <passphrase>
  ifconfig /dev/net/rtl8814au/0 auto-config

This driver is NOT part of the official Haiku distribution.  It is
developed independently and shipped as a standalone package.  Bug reports
welcome at https://github.com/KevinAdams05/rtl8814au_unofficial/issues."

